      "comment": "Rewrite Overview page copy to be more accessible / marketing-friendly\nAvoid assuming users know terms like “Critical Success Criteria” or “National Action Plan”.\nSuggested direction: language like “assessing Australia’s industrial regions on their progress towards clean industry”, then explain that the NAP assesses 16 regions against shared criteria.\n\nGO to our website to see how we are describing this work. at www.bae.org.au\n\nI have also pasted our 2 pager that we used for the London Climate Action week to brief an international audience on this work. This is the most current way we are describing this work. Don't copy it work for word, but use it for inspiration and apply it for this work.",
      "target": {
        "selector": "div.hero:nth-of-type(2)",
        "tag": "div",
        "elementId": "",
        "classes": "hero",
        "text": "Beyond Zero Emissions Assessing Australia's industrial regions against the Critical Success Criteria The National Action Plan assesses each region against a shared set of indicators across five themes, scoring every one from 1 to 5 against its own grading scale. Each score is backed by published evi",
        "html": "<div class=\"hero\"> <div class=\"eyebrow\">Beyond Zero Emissions</div> <h1>Assessing Australia's industrial regions against the Critical Success Criteria</h1> <p class=\"lede\">The National Action Plan assesses each region against a shared set of indicators across five themes, scoring every one from 1 to 5 against its own grading scale. Each score is backed by published evidence.</p> <div class=\"tiles\" id=\"tiles\"><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"tileN\">16</div><div class=\"tileL\">regions in scope</div></div><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"tileN\">4</div><div class=\"tileL\">with an assessment</div></div><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"tileN\">50</div><div class=\"tileL\">indicators per region</div></div><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"tileN\">44<sup>%</sup></div><div class=\"tileL\">assessed regions scored<br>87 of 200 region–indicator pairs</div></div></div> </div>",
